# OCM — protective ignore rules.
#
# This directory is intended to be open-sourced, so the posture is deliberately
# excessive: it is cheap to un-ignore a file later, and impossible to un-publish a
# secret. Anything describing THIS deployment (account ids, endpoints, instance ids)
# is treated as sensitive even when it is not strictly a credential.
#
# Note: ignoring a file does not protect a secret written INSIDE a committed file.
# `tests/no-secrets.test.mjs` enforces that part.

# ---- credentials, keys, tokens ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc
.envrc.*
.direnv/
# Templates are the exception: placeholders only, and the secret scan enforces that.
!.env.example
!.envrc.example
!.deploy.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
.ssh/
.aws/
.gnupg/
credentials
credentials.*
*credential*.csv
*accessKeys*.csv
*.csv
secrets/
private/
kubeconfig*
.netrc

# ---- deployment-specific state ------------------------------------------------
# Account ids, instance ids and endpoints identify our infrastructure.
.deploy.env
deployment.json
inventory.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform/
cdk.out/
.serverless/
.pulumi/

# ---- runtime data -------------------------------------------------------------
# The ledger holds account ids and usage.
.data/
*.jsonl
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
dump.rdb

# ---- documentation ------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ is the operator's notebook: live account ids, hostnames, instance ids,
# emails. It is written for us, not for readers, and is excluded wholesale.
docs/
# Everything else defaults to excluded, with the conventional public set allowed
# back in. Those files are written deliberately for publication; anything new is
# excluded until someone decides otherwise.
*.md
!README.md
!LICENSE.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!CHANGELOG.md

# ---- captured output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Browser-driver screenshots can contain a logged-in AWS console.
shots/
screenshots/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
*.har
*.pcap

# ---- build and local noise ----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
*.log
logs/
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
tmp/
.tmp/
.cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.bak
*.orig
*~
